This proposed multi-player hack (I suggest "MultHack") would indeed be
complex.  Either the idea of a party of adventurers could be used, or
separate questers, with a few changes:

1) Attacking a co-aligned human is a Big No-No with the gods.
2) So is attacking a human of a level more than two below yours.
3) Add a "pickpocket" spell to steal items from other characters/creatures
4) Timing's simple.  One cycle per second, no paralysis or sleep longer than
   sixty seconds.  Other effects can be scaled.
5) Add an inter-player communication feature to #chat.  Add a way to give
   items directly to another (other than dropping them)
6) When a player dies, the level IMMEDIATELY becomes a bones level so the
   other players currently in the game can find the dead guy's stuff
7) If you wish to save your game, you enter a simple routine to automate
   your character while you're not there... (e.g. a "cyborg", as in muds,
   a simple program like "Attack anything that hits me.  Run away if my HP
   drops below 1/4 of full.  Pick up only artifacts and blessed objects.
   Cast spells and refresh them as necessary.")  This lets others attack the
   character and have him/her stand a chance of survival.
8) Ascended characters become "demigods" in a realer sense and can
   influence the game.  They can try to get worshipers (by making altars to
   themselves, and offering players more goodies for worshiping them) and can
   thus become minor gods, then full gods.  Gods' players may choose to leave
   their god character as a normal automated god and begin again as mortals.
9) Split character class/race!  "Elf" is not a class - it's a species.  Add
   Dwarves and some others as potential races.  Add more classes.  (Esper for
   one)

Simple.

